  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to earthquake in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On February 6, 2023, two powerful earthquakes hit southeast Turkey and Syria, causing the destruction of homes, schools, hospitals. The affected areas are also facing harsh winter conditions, with temperatures dropping below freezing. Without immediate action, children suffer the most, including trauma, loss of access to basic services, separation and increased risks of exploitation and abuse.
The response is designed to address the needs of most affected children&amp;nbsp;and their families in Aleppo and Lattakia: 1) provide PFA&amp;nbsp;to children and caregivers, 2) provide PSS &amp;amp; SPSS for children, 3) Distribute&amp;nbsp;children&apos;s kits (diapers, wet wipes, blanket etc) 3) distribute&amp;nbsp;multi-purpose cash.</narrative>
  </description>
